  'guide.hero.d': 'An end-to-end guide to Musico — from first install, folders, and multi-queues to swipe gestures, synced lyrics, custom themes, Cloud Hangouts, and official plugins (ﾉ◕ヮ◕)ﾉ*:･ﾟ✧',

  'guide.install.t': 'Downloads, First-Run Setup & In-App Updates',
  'guide.install.p': 'Grab the latest builds directly below or from GitHub Releases. Every release includes <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> and an in-app updater on desktop &amp; Android.',
  'guide.install.li1': '<strong>Windows 10 / 11 (x64, self-contained .NET 8):</strong> Run <code>MusicoWindows-&lt;ver&gt;-win-x64-Setup.exe</code> for per-user install with Start Menu / Desktop shortcuts, system tray, and single-instance focus — or unzip <code>MusicoWindows-&lt;ver&gt;-win-x64-portable.zip</code> anywhere and keep <code>portable.txt</code> beside <code>MusicoWindows.exe</code> so your library, queues, extensions, and settings live inside <code>.\\Data\\</code> instead of <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Musico</code>.',
  'guide.install.li2': '<strong>Android 8.0+ (API 26+):</strong> Install the persistently signed <code>MusicoAndroid-&lt;ver&gt;-release.apk</code> so in-app <code>FileProvider</code> upgrades install smoothly without losing data (or grab <code>debug.apk</code> for local testing).',
  'guide.install.li3': '<strong>macOS (Catalyst):</strong> Open <code>Musico-&lt;ver&gt;-macOS.dmg</code> and drag <code>Musico.app</code> into <code>Applications</code>. Because builds are ad-hoc signed, right-click then choose <strong>Open</strong> on first launch if Gatekeeper asks.',
  'guide.install.li4': '<strong>iOS 17+ / iPadOS:</strong> Sideload or re-sign <code>Musico-&lt;ver&gt;-iOS-unsigned.ipa</code> using AltStore, SideStore, Sideloadly, or Xcode.',
  'guide.install.upT': 'In-App Updater & Checksum Verification',
  'guide.install.up1': '<strong>Check for Updates:</strong> Desktop (Windows Setup/Portable &amp; macOS) and Android clients automatically poll GitHub <code>releases/latest</code>, or you can trigger a check manually from Settings.',
  'guide.install.up2': '<strong>Skip Version or Upgrade:</strong> Choose <strong>Skip Version</strong> to silence a specific release banner, or proceed to download — Windows and Android verify <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code> before launching the self-replacing Portable zip, Setup installer, or Android <code>FileProvider</code> installer (macOS downloads and opens the new <code>.dmg</code>).',
  'guide.install.up3': '<strong>iOS Note:</strong> Because personal-team sideloaded IPAs cannot self-update in place, re-sign and install new <code>.ipa</code> releases via AltStore, SideStore, Sideloadly, or Xcode.',

  'guide.folders.t': 'Folders, Scanning, Relocate & Safe Deletion',
  'guide.folders.p': 'Musico treats your directory tree as the source of truth — never flattening folders into a black-box database.',
  'guide.folders.roots': '<strong>OS Default Roots:</strong> macOS starts with <code>Music</code>; iOS/iPadOS watches <code>Files › On My iPhone/iPad › Musico</code>; Android uses <code>Musico Folder</code> plus any Storage Access Framework (SAF) directory; Windows starts with <code>MyMusic</code> (or <code>.\\Data\\</code> in Portable mode).',
  'guide.folders.stepsT': 'Day-to-Day Folder Workflow',
  'guide.folders.s1': '<strong>Mount Local Folders:</strong> Open <strong>Folders → Add Folder</strong> to pick any local or SAF directory without copying or altering your subfolders.',
  'guide.folders.s2': '<strong>Rescan for New Tracks:</strong> Tap <strong>Rescan</strong> (or pull to refresh on iOS/Android) whenever you add new audio files to a mounted folder.',
  'guide.folders.s3': '<strong>Desktop Drag-and-Drop:</strong> Drop folders onto the macOS or Windows window to mount them directly in <strong>Folders</strong>, or drop audio files to play immediately (tracks outside your library copy neatly into your default music folder).',
  'guide.folders.s4': '<strong>Relocate &amp; Restore Subfolders:</strong> Moved a folder or unplugged an external drive? Pick <strong>Locate Again… (Relocate)</strong> to reconnect the path while keeping playlists, queue history, and play stats intact. Hidden a subfolder by mistake? Use <strong>Restore Removed Subfolders</strong> anytime.',
  'guide.folders.s5': "<strong>Remove vs. Delete on Disk:</strong> Removing a track or folder gives an explicit choice — <strong>Remove from Library</strong> (hides it from Musico only) or disk deletion (<strong>Move to Trash</strong> on macOS, <strong>Move to Recycle Bin</strong> on Windows, or <strong>Delete from Device</strong> on iOS/Android, including Android's <code>Musico</code> folder).",
